From bc9c8c418b582edd067288599b69b47d593fa378 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:39:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 31/45] Built-in MCP server (Preferences > MCP Server)

An MCP server inside KiCad (Streamable HTTP with JSON responses), so Claude Code
or another MCP client can read and change the design while the user watches.
Clients connect to http://127.0.0.1:27880/mcp, or to the device's Wi-Fi address,
with a Bearer token.  The server is off until it is turned on.

- api_server: HandleRequest() runs IPC API requests in process
- api/src/kiapi_json.cpp: JSON <-> API messages, inside libkiapi, where the
  message descriptors are (libprotobuf is linked into several libraries)
- mcp_server: the HTTP server, JSON-RPC, and the tools: kicad_status,
  kicad_open_editor, kicad_api, kicad_api_commands, kicad_api_describe, and
  pcb_board_summary, pcb_move_footprint, pcb_run_drc and pcb_autoroute, whose
  handlers the board editor attaches while it is open
- panel_mcp_server: on/off, this device or another computer, the address and
  ready-to-paste claude commands with Copy buttons, a live status line, port and
  new token
- dialog_autoroute: ImportAutorouteSession() shared with pcb_autoroute

